1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,758
The buyer wanted midnight delivery. One
minute past, he tried to keep

2
00:00:04,758 --> 00:00:06,740
Jason and Lucia's fee too.

3
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:11,101
Earlier, Lucia had read the freight
elevator's weight limit. The case

4
00:00:11,101 --> 00:00:13,480
could ride safely. Both couriers
couldn't.

5
00:00:13,480 --> 00:00:18,238
Jason stepped out beside her. They sent
the sealed case upstairs alone,

6
00:00:18,238 --> 00:00:20,220
then climbed the warehouse's stairs.

7
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:25,374
Above them, the delivery bell rang.
Through a window, Lucia saw the clock:

8
00:00:25,374 --> 00:00:26,960
one minute before midnight.

9
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:31,715
They reached their buyer. His smile was
enormous. Late arrivals didn't get

10
00:00:31,715 --> 00:00:33,300
paid, he told them.

11
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:37,659
Lucia pointed at his delivery receipt.
The building's caretaker had signed

12
00:00:37,659 --> 00:00:40,830
for the case when the elevator bell
rang.

13
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:45,586
He'd bought delivery, not their company.
Jason held out his hand. The

14
00:00:45,586 --> 00:00:48,360
buyer counted their full fee into it.

15
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:53,029
They took the stairs down together.
Lucia kept the receipt. Jason

16
00:00:53,029 --> 00:00:56,000
complained that work had too many steps.
